Red — my test caught a real bug! The function-valued source is validated against a STALE schema. Why?

Look at `validatorFor(name, schema)`: caches by schema object in WeakMap. Each `resolveDefinition()` call returns a NEW definition object (function source returns a fresh literal each call) — so schema object differs each call → WeakMap miss → compile fresh. That should work...

But the failure says: FIRST call (`execute('shape_shifter', {})`) rejected with "input.lastName is required" — i.e., the FIRST call already used schema generation 2 (lastName)!

Why? `resolved` increments... AH — `getDefinitions()`? No. What calls resolveDefinition multiple times per execute? `execute`: resolveDefinition once → schema gen N. Hmm — but WAIT: the FIRST execute call happens after... `register` — register calls `resolveDefinition(definition)` too! (line: `const resolved = this.resolveDefinition(definition);`) — that consumes generation 1 at REGISTER time. Then execute #1 resolves generation 2 (lastName schema) → `{}` rejected for lastName. So my counter design is off: register consumes one resolution.

